hands, wash your hands.


01:08:32.642 --> 01:08:36.945
I'm her sister, Lily, and this
our older sister Vera here.


01:08:36.947 --> 01:08:38.179
- Hiya.


01:08:38.181 --> 01:08:39.481
- That's Jason, my husband.


01:08:39.483 --> 01:08:40.949
- Sorry about the door.


01:08:40.951 --> 01:08:42.851
- This little one
here is grace, my daughter,


01:08:42.853 --> 01:08:44.285
and my older daughter,
Tara, is probably running


01:08:44.287 --> 01:08:45.420
around out back somewhere.


01:08:45.422 --> 01:08:47.288
- I believe you.


01:08:47.290 --> 01:08:49.757
- You're here to rescue me?


01:08:49.759 --> 01:08:52.260
- Rescue you from what?


01:08:52.262 --> 01:08:54.062
- Somebody at the door?


01:08:54.064 --> 01:08:56.364
- You're in trouble,
dad's coming.


01:08:56.366 --> 01:09:01.102
Hey, pops, Susan has someone
she wants you to meet.


01:09:01.104 --> 01:09:02.237
This is Sam.


01:09:07.009 --> 01:09:09.244
- He can stay for dinner.


01:09:20.156 --> 01:09:21.322
- They're just so cute.


01:09:21.324 --> 01:09:23.224
- Yeah, they're cute.


01:09:24.293 --> 01:09:25.860
- You just wanna eat 'em up.


01:09:25.862 --> 01:09:27.095
You know, just something so cute


01:09:27.097 --> 01:09:29.764
you just wanna eat it all up?


01:09:29.766 --> 01:09:32.500
Like chop it into a salad.


01:09:32.502 --> 01:09:35.970
Their little fingers, little
ears, just eat 'em up.


01:09:35.972 --> 01:09:36.972
- Yeah, I got ya.


01:09:41.010 --> 01:09:42.277
- You take my little girl


01:09:42.279 --> 01:09:45.547
and I'll chop you up
into little pieces.


01:09:46.982 --> 01:09:49.617
Wait, that come out wrong.


01:09:49.619 --> 01:09:51.252
I don't mean 'cause you're cute.


01:09:51.254 --> 01:09:52.587
- No, right.


01:09:52.589 --> 01:09:54.689
- I meant the part about
taking my little girl.


01:09:54.691 --> 01:09:58.159
- I understand what
you were telling me.


01:10:05.568 --> 01:10:07.936
- Ooh, it's a beauty.


01:10:07.938 --> 01:10:09.571
- Oh, she's done it again.


01:10:09.573 --> 01:10:11.940
- Mmm, look at that.


01:10:13.976 --> 01:10:14.976
- Mmm.


01:10:16.212 --> 01:10:18.613
- Dad, you wanna say grace?


01:10:22.751 --> 01:10:26.154
- God, we thank you for
the blessing of this food,


01:10:26.156 --> 01:10:27.622
and this family.


01:10:28.857 --> 01:10:30.825
Couldn't bring my
Lorna back to me,


01:10:30.827 --> 01:10:33.528
but you brung Susie back


01:10:33.530 --> 01:10:36.731
and it's like Lorna's
here in spirit.


01:10:38.100 --> 01:10:39.567
- Amen.


01:10:39.569 --> 01:10:43.938
- And lord, thank you so
much for this nice young man.


01:10:43.940 --> 01:10:47.775
Maybe he'll make an honest
woman of my little girl one day.


01:10:47.777 --> 01:10:49.277
- Dad!


01:10:49.279 --> 01:10:51.980
- I'm just saying, you're
a good guy, welcome.


01:10:51.982 --> 01:10:52.982
- Thanks.


01:10:55.217 --> 01:10:58.853
- Now, son, the way
I carve these things,


01:11:00.656 --> 01:11:04.259
what I like to do is
start with the leg.


01:11:04.261 --> 01:11:06.828
- Ooh, look how juicy.


01:11:07.863 --> 01:11:10.098
- These two have such
a nice aura about them.


01:11:10.100 --> 01:11:11.633
- Don't they?


01:11:11.635 --> 01:11:14.269
You could stay here, Jason
could help you get a job.


01:11:14.271 --> 01:11:16.271
- Maybe some sort
of a starter job.


01:11:16.273 --> 01:11:18.072
- He can't just leave
his practice behind,


01:11:18.074 --> 01:11:19.274
he's got patients.


01:11:19.276 --> 01:11:20.341
- You're a doctor?


01:11:20.343 --> 01:11:22.076
- He's a therapist.


01:11:24.913 --> 01:11:27.715
- I'm an occupational therapist.


01:11:29.218 --> 01:11:32.253
I help people in the
place they occupy.


01:11:32.255 --> 01:11:36.057
- Well, there's plenty
of crazy people here.


01:11:37.293 --> 01:11:39.994
- Yeah, I dunno, maybe I could.


01:11:41.964 --> 01:11:43.865
- What about all your patients?


01:11:43.867 --> 01:11:45.500
- We don't wanna
lose our Susie again.


01:11:45.502 --> 01:11:48.469
- Seems like we're
always losing our Susie.


01:11:48.471 --> 01:11:50.471
Remember that time in the field?


01:11:50.473 --> 01:11:53.374
- Oh god, mom almost
had a nervous breakdown.


01:11:53.376 --> 01:11:54.442
She was sick.


01:11:54.444 --> 01:11:57.211
- Dad, tell the story.


01:11:57.213 --> 01:11:59.514
- It was back when I was
still driving the truck


01:11:59.516 --> 01:12:02.650
before the sciatica
made me useless.


01:12:03.886 --> 01:12:06.421
I was coming through
Iowa, and on the Cb


01:12:06.423 --> 01:12:11.125
Susie's mother told me that
Susie's lost in the corn.


01:12:11.127 --> 01:12:12.760
Yeah.


01:12:12.762 --> 01:12:14.929
Never so scared in my
life, I put the pedal down


01:12:14.931 --> 01:12:17.832
on the floor, and grinding
the hell out of the gears.


01:12:17.834 --> 01:12:20.568
I got here in two hours.


01:12:20.570 --> 01:12:23.604
Pulled up right on my lawn.


01:12:23.606 --> 01:12:26.407
I was hugging her crying mother.


01:12:27.443 --> 01:12:28.943
I didn't notice how
high the corn was,


01:12:28.945 --> 01:12:30.878
if we went in there,
we'd never even be able


01:12:30.880 --> 01:12:32.580
to find each other.


01:12:33.849 --> 01:12:37.418
A couple of moments
later, like a vision,


01:12:40.122 --> 01:12:43.624
she was walking
out of the cornrows


01:12:43.626 --> 01:12:46.027
in her little summer dress.


01:12:47.429 --> 01:12:51.065
Even then she looked
just like her mother.


01:12:56.605 --> 01:12:59.307
- It must tear
you up with guilt.


01:12:59.309 --> 01:13:00.541
- Well, we found her.


01:13:00.543 --> 01:13:02.343
All's well that ends well.


01:13:02.345 --> 01:13:05.046
- No I mean, the mother, Lorna.


01:13:06.982 --> 01:13:08.349
- Guilty about what?


01:13:08.351 --> 01:13:11.586
- After she, after
you, well, I mean,


01:13:13.088 --> 01:13:15.890
it wasn't on purpose, it
was an accident, sort of.


01:13:15.892 --> 01:13:18.359
- What was an accident.


01:13:18.361 --> 01:13:20.361
- When he killed her.


01:13:20.363 --> 01:13:21.363
- Susan?


01:13:23.298 --> 01:13:24.365
- He's right, we all know.


01:13:24.367 --> 01:13:25.333
- Dad, don't say that.


01:13:25.335 --> 01:13:27.468
- Come on, kids.


01:13:30.906 --> 01:13:32.573
- What did you tell him?


01:13:32.575 --> 01:13:34.108
- I couldn't give
her what she needed.


01:13:34.110 --> 01:13:35.243
- Dad, don't say that.


01:13:35.245 --> 01:13:36.544
- I didn't love her hard enough.


01:13:36.546 --> 01:13:37.712
- Dad, it was the cancer.


01:13:37.714 --> 01:13:39.280
- Dad, please don't
get sad again.


01:13:39.282 --> 01:13:42.316
Mom's here with us tonight,
you said so yourself.


01:13:42.318 --> 01:13:43.584
- Cancer?


01:13:43.586 --> 01:13:44.919
- What did she tell you?


01:13:44.921 --> 01:13:46.087
- You told me he killed her.


01:13:46.089 --> 01:13:47.989
- I know it, he's right.


01:13:47.991 --> 01:13:49.624
- Dad, you did not kill mom.


01:13:49.626 --> 01:13:50.858
- Did you say that?


01:13:50.860 --> 01:13:52.093
- Of course not.


01:13:52.095 --> 01:13:52.960
- Why would you
say such a thing?


01:13:52.962 --> 01:13:54.295
- It's not true.


01:13:54.297 --> 01:13:57.598
- I'm sorry, I, I
must have misheard.


01:13:57.600 --> 01:13:58.800
- Jeez, dad.


01:13:59.868 --> 01:14:03.471
- No no no no please,
it's okay, it's okay.


01:14:23.258 --> 01:14:26.360
- I came here to rescue
you from a psychotic man


01:14:26.362 --> 01:14:30.665
who you ran away from, but
it was just another story.


01:14:32.034 --> 01:14:33.668
- What do you care, you
don't know these people.


01:14:33.670 --> 01:14:35.670
- I feel humiliated.


01:14:35.672 --> 01:14:36.671
They hate me.


01:14:36.673 --> 01:14:38.539
- You lied to me too.


01:14:47.282 --> 01:14:49.884
- When I was in third
grade, I was convinced


01:14:49.886 --> 01:14:53.187
my math teacher Mr.
Barney was my dad.


01:14:54.223 --> 01:14:58.292
He had a little limp, so
I started limping too.


01:15:00.028 --> 01:15:01.562
When I was in fourth
grade, I was sure


01:15:01.564 --> 01:15:06.133
is was my gym teacher, so I
lost the limp for a strut.


01:15:06.135 --> 01:15:09.604
I remember believing
it was the mailman.


01:15:11.073 --> 01:15:15.309
Local beat cops, guys at
stores, any grown up man


01:15:15.311 --> 01:15:17.211
I met more than once.


01:15:19.014 --> 01:15:22.517
Then one day, my mom was
working some late shift


01:15:22.519 --> 01:15:25.753
on a third job, and I was
going through her closet,


01:15:25.755 --> 01:15:30.057
I found the book, the photo
slipped out, and I just...


01:15:35.230 --> 01:15:39.367
I get it, it was just
easier, but I believed it.


01:15:42.104 --> 01:15:44.338
It's stupid, I see that.


01:15:44.340 --> 01:15:47.575
- It's even worse,
you lied to yourself.


01:15:47.577 --> 01:15:48.409
- At least I have a reason.


01:15:48.411 --> 01:15:49.844
- I had a reason.


01:15:49.846 --> 01:15:52.446
- A reason for calling
your own father a murderer?


01:15:52.448 --> 01:15:54.749
- You said it yourself.


01:15:54.751 --> 01:15:59.053
You only followed me
because you believed me.


01:15:59.055 --> 01:16:00.154
- So I came.


01:16:02.157 --> 01:16:03.457
Why am I here?


01:16:08.030 --> 01:16:09.764
- You shouldn't be.


01:16:14.436 --> 01:16:17.672
- Is somebody gonna
apologize to dad?


01:16:19.675 --> 01:16:22.176
- You didn't do
anything, you know that.


01:16:22.178 --> 01:16:26.314
- Hey, I just wanna say,
I think I got confused.


01:16:29.117 --> 01:16:31.385
I have a lot of patients.


01:16:31.387 --> 01:16:35.189
Sometimes I get stories
mixed up in my head.


01:16:36.224 --> 01:16:38.426
I realize now that
something one of


01:16:38.428 --> 01:16:40.928
my patients said, not Susan.


01:16:40.930 --> 01:16:43.197
- You ruined dinner.


01:16:43.199 --> 01:16:45.666
- Hey, he comes in peace.


01:16:45.668 --> 01:16:47.501
- Look, it's not a family meal


01:16:47.503 --> 01:16:50.304
unless there's a dust up or two.


01:16:51.006 --> 01:16:52.740
It's not a big deal.


01:16:52.742 --> 01:16:53.808
Don't worry about it.


01:16:53.810 --> 01:16:55.042
- There you go.


01:16:55.044 --> 01:16:57.078
Daddy, will you
play guitar for us?


01:16:57.080 --> 01:16:58.679
- Okay.


01:16:58.681 --> 01:17:01.716
- Jeez, then I'll build a fire.


01:17:59.007 --> 01:18:00.374
- You can sing.


01:18:01.376 --> 01:18:04.178
- It's her voice, I swear.


01:18:04.180 --> 01:18:06.814
- It's like she's back.


01:19:09.177 --> 01:19:12.313
- She's the prettiest
of all of 'em.


01:19:15.550 --> 01:19:19.286
She looks so much like
her mom I could cry.


01:19:24.326 --> 01:19:27.128
I'm not ready to lose her again.


01:19:30.532 --> 01:19:34.602
I'm not ready to let you
take her away from me.


01:19:40.542 --> 01:19:42.343
Don't take her away.


01:20:38.500 --> 01:20:41.068
- It's morning, it's morning!


01:20:41.070 --> 01:20:42.369
- Tara, cut that out.


01:20:42.371 --> 01:20:43.938
Sorry about that.


01:21:03.458 --> 01:21:05.159
- Making breakfast?


01:21:08.363 --> 01:21:10.764
- No one else will make it.


01:21:24.746 --> 01:21:26.714
- What's in your hair?


01:21:28.250 --> 01:21:30.451
- Why are you still here?


01:21:36.258 --> 01:21:40.561
- Your father, last night,
he was in the hallway, he...


01:21:42.297 --> 01:21:43.597
- Look at you.


01:21:46.234 --> 01:21:47.234
Dad, look.


01:21:56.111 --> 01:21:58.312
- Where did you get this?


01:21:59.180 --> 01:22:01.649
- I kept it in my drawer.


01:22:01.651 --> 01:22:03.851
You don't like it?


01:22:03.853 --> 01:22:05.319
- What is it?


01:22:05.321 --> 01:22:07.821
- It was mom's.


01:22:07.823 --> 01:22:10.791
Doesn't she look beautiful?


01:22:10.793 --> 01:22:12.660
- I need some coffee.


01:22:28.410 --> 01:22:30.644
- So how did you two meet?


01:22:30.646 --> 01:22:31.612
- We were at a baseball game...


01:22:31.614 --> 01:22:33.380
- we were on the train.


01:22:33.382 --> 01:22:35.983
- Well, which is it?


01:22:35.985 --> 01:22:38.118
- Her hand brushed mine.


01:22:39.454 --> 01:22:42.356
When I felt that touch,
that was all I needed.


01:22:42.358 --> 01:22:45.159
I followed her home, I
would have followed her


01:22:45.161 --> 01:22:46.460
to the gates of hell.


01:22:46.462 --> 01:22:48.162
- Aw, that's sweet.


01:22:48.164 --> 01:22:49.363
- Bit creepy.


01:23:05.981 --> 01:23:08.615
- I just thought of something.


01:23:13.588 --> 01:23:17.791
Do you remember, we took a
road trip, it was my idea.


01:23:17.793 --> 01:23:20.527
It was an unusually warm April.


01:23:21.896 --> 01:23:24.732
I said I can get us a car.


01:23:24.734 --> 01:23:28.635
Let's go to the dells,
let's go camping.


01:23:28.637 --> 01:23:32.006
You said it might
rain, but I insisted.


01:23:33.875 --> 01:23:35.342
Do you remember?


01:23:41.016 --> 01:23:44.151
- The forecasts,
they all said rain.


01:23:46.955 --> 01:23:50.457
- I was stubborn, I
get a tent of storage,


01:23:50.459 --> 01:23:51.959
I borrow a car for work.


01:23:51.961 --> 01:23:53.794
- You threw out the cigarette
lighter so I wouldn't smoke.


01:23:53.796 --> 01:23:54.695
- I'm not gonna
think about that now,


01:23:54.697 --> 01:23:56.730
I hate myself for that.


01:23:57.966 --> 01:24:00.434
I had to control everything.


01:24:00.436 --> 01:24:03.137
- You wanted me to be the best.


01:24:05.540 --> 01:24:08.642
- We sit in that tent
for three straight days,


01:24:08.644 --> 01:24:11.512
it never stopped raining, we
never stopped playing cards.


01:24:11.514 --> 01:24:13.380
- Gin rummy and I
beat you every hand.


01:24:13.382 --> 01:24:14.782
- God, I got so angry.


01:24:14.784 --> 01:24:16.417
- You like to win.


01:24:17.352 --> 01:24:19.586
- I wanna go back.


01:24:19.588 --> 01:24:22.489
I wanna put you in the car.


01:24:22.491 --> 01:24:25.626
I wanna save you from
the mud, and the wet.


01:24:25.628 --> 01:24:26.960
I wanna roll up the tent.


01:24:26.962 --> 01:24:29.830
- Leave the tent,
it's all muddy.


01:24:29.832 --> 01:24:33.867
- Stop at a diner on the 94,
get some hot split pea soup.


01:24:33.869 --> 01:24:34.802
- I hate split pea soup.


01:24:34.804 --> 01:24:35.903
- You like split pea soup.


01:24:35.905 --> 01:24:37.438
- No I don't.


01:24:37.440 --> 01:24:39.573
- I wanna make you warm.


01:24:40.642 --> 01:24:42.609
I wanna take you home.


01:24:43.611 --> 01:24:44.611
- Please.

